      "fixturesBytes": 3905,
      "deviations": [
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/GitHubRepository.test.ts; scratchpad/test/github/GitHubClient.test.ts; scratchpad/test/github/resources2.test.ts; module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "GitHubRepository.SECURITY_ANALYSIS_STATUS_FIELDS and GitHubError/Issue membership use native Set; CodeScanning, GitHubApp, GitHubRepository and TokenPermissions use Object keys/entries/hasOwn; CheckRun uses wall-clock Date and WorkflowDispatch wraps Clock millis in Date.",
          "labBehaviour": "These sites use HashSet and Record helpers. SECURITY_ANALYSIS_STATUS_FIELDS exposes HashSet. CheckRun.started_at/completed_at and WorkflowDispatch dispatch time use DateTime.now/formatIso; check timestamps now follow the Effect clock. Native error replacements are recorded under tagged-errors.",
          "reason": "native-runtime: Beep native-runtime law and the 2026-10-09 recording/public-API ruling require Effect collections, Record and DateTime; INVENTORY codemod-02 identifies clock and public collection changes. Github had no allowlist entries to remove."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/GitHubClient.test.ts:557; scratchpad/test/github/GitHubClient.test.ts:646; scratchpad/test/github/transport.test.ts:93; module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "Resource makeTest members throw native Error; missing request, pagination and GraphQL fixtures die with native Error. The Octokit attempt catches raw unknown throwables.",
          "labBehaviour": "Resource files, including CheckRun, GitHubClient, GitHubRepository and GitHubCommit, use S.TaggedError UnstubbedError; GitHubClient uses FixtureError. internal/octokit uses TransportFailure with S.Defect before classification, preserving cause identity. CommitFileDecodeError was removed.",
          "reason": "tagged-errors: Beep law 7 and D5 require schema-tagged errors; INVENTORY codemod-01 and req-31, fix-github-g7.md:3. Existing messages and fixture defect channels survive; typed external commit decoding is recorded under effect-first."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/CodeScanning.test.ts:112; scratchpad/test/github/GitHubRepository.test.ts:334; scratchpad/test/github/Ruleset.test.ts:233; scratchpad/test/github/resources2.test.ts:635; module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "CodeScanningSetup, DeploymentEnvironmentInfo, AppliedSettings, UpsertedPullRequest, SecretInfo, VariableInfo, RulesetInfo, RulesetPayload and WorkflowInfo are erased interfaces; named literal domains use S.Literals; status membership is handwritten and accepts arrays with a status property; tests parse JSON directly.",
          "labBehaviour": "The nine models gain Struct schemas and derived types, keeping open fields and plain objects. CheckConclusion, AnnotationLevel, FileMode, FileStatus, GitHubErrorKind, GitHubValidationCode, MergeMethod, PermissionLevel and RequestMethod use LiteralKit. StatusObject uses S.is and rejects arrays; tests/reachability use fromJsonString codecs.",
          "reason": "schema-first: D5, schema-first ownership, law 17 and law 19/EF-12b force runtime models, derived guards, named LiteralKit domains and JSON codecs; fix-github-g1/g2/g3/g4/g5/g6/g7 and INVENTORY req-06/07/20/22/26/27/28. RulesetPayload remains upstream-open; array rejection is law-forced."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/Ruleset.test.ts:246; scratchpad/test/github/WorkflowDispatch.test.ts:196; module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "RulesetInfo.id and WorkflowInfo.id are number fields on interfaces, with no owning runtime numeric validator.",
          "labBehaviour": "Ruleset.ts RulesetInfo.id and WorkflowDispatch.ts WorkflowInfo.id use S.Finite in the new boundary schemas; the TypeScript fields remain number. Existing integer constraints elsewhere are retained.",
          "reason": "numeric-domains: schemaNumber TS377098 requires finite numeric domains when the schema-first models are introduced; fix-github-g5.md:27 supplies the diagnostic cause. D5 and the per-module numeric-domain recording ruling apply."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/GitHubClient.test.ts:631; scratchpad/test/github/GitHubClient.test.ts:759; scratchpad/test/github/Ruleset.test.ts:205; scratchpad/test/github/GitHubRepository.test.ts:159; scratchpad/test/github/transport.test.ts:84",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "GitHubClient fixtures hold raw unknown payloads/errors and cast them to route data; empty single requests fabricate {} as A. Route writes, throwable guards, pagination and tests use casts, assertions or diagnostic suppressions; thrown header arrays can supply rate-limit properties.",
          "labBehaviour": "GitHubFixtures request/paginate are route-keyed Result values; requestDecoded has its own raw bucket. Empty single requests fail notFound, while pagination stays empty. Typed request overloads, property narrowing, safe spreads and Ruleset requestDecoded remove casts; deliberatelyInvalid owns wrong-input casts. Thrown header arrays no longer update snapshots; touched suppressions are removed.",
          "reason": "type-safety: D15 and the 2026-10-09 deliberatelyInvalid ruling; INVENTORY codemod-05, req-25/29/30 and fix-github-g3/g4/g6/g7. Law 17 requires built-in narrowing instead of the unsound array-to-record guard. Deferred suppressions elsewhere remain backlog-03."
        },
        {
          "test": "module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "CodeScanning.languages, DeploymentEnvironment.list, RepositoryVariable.list, Ruleset.list and three RepositorySecurity reads are zero-argument Effect functions; internal crypto, headers and pagination helpers expose only data-first calls. Classes/errors use constructor calls.",
          "labBehaviour": "The listed members are Effect values with deferred stubs. GitHubRepository settings/ownerType use effect-valued generators with restored spans. encryptSecret, headerString/headerNumber/retryAfterMillisFrom and paginate/fromArray expose dual overloads; schema classes/errors use make, and typed decoding follows diagnostic-compatible forms.",
          "reason": "tsgo-diagnostics: @effect/tsgo lazyEffect, effectFnIife, missingPipeableSignature, newSchemaClass and typed-decoding diagnostics; INVENTORY codemod-04 and actual S0 diff. Numeric schemaNumber changes are consolidated under numeric-domains."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/resources.test.ts:446; scratchpad/test/github/resources.test.ts:463; scratchpad/test/github/resources2.test.ts:589; scratchpad/test/github/GitHubRepository.test.ts:39; module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "withCheckRun, GitTag.reset, GitBranch.readRef and client/transport factories wrap Effect.gen; helpers retain trivial decoder/success/None wrappers. GitHubCommit.fileOf synchronously constructs CommitFile, so malformed external status throws a schema defect at compare, changedFiles and PullRequest.listFiles.",
          "labBehaviour": "The wrappers use Effect.fn/fnUntraced and direct helpers; Option getSomesStruct preserves optional wire fields and scoped Layer construction supplies tests through provideContext. fileOf is effectful and traversed with Effect.forEach, mapping invalid file data to operation-specific GitHubError.decode with cause. Repository resource spans remain preserved.",
          "reason": "effect-first: Beep effect-fn/terse-effect laws, EF-3 external typed error boundaries and explicit service/layer ownership; INVENTORY req-04/23/24/32 and fix-github-g1.md:18. The invalid-status change is law-forced, not a separate upstream-bug entry."
        },
        {
          "test": "module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "Source, tests and examples import Effect modules from the root effect barrel.",
          "labBehaviour": "Github source, tests and examples import each module through effect/Effect, effect/Schema, effect/Context and other module paths; Function helpers use effect/Function. Option and LiteralKit integration use existing Beep subpaths.",
          "reason": "effect-imports: Operator step 3 and the effect-imports law require per-module Effect imports; the S0 diff covers source, tests and examples."
        },
        {
          "test": "module suite scratchpad/test/github/**",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "Schema identifiers are short local names, schema fields lack the port metadata, and Context.Service keys use @effected/github strings.",
          "labBehaviour": "Source schemas and services use $ScratchpadId.create(effected/github/<file>), composed $I identifiers, annote/annoteSchema and field descriptions; retained error schemas and new boundary models receive owning metadata, including RulesetInfo/Payload and TransportFailure.",
          "reason": "identity-annotations: Operator step 4 and D5 require @beep/identity identities and schema/field annotations; fix-github-g1/g3/g4/g7 and INVENTORY req-08/09/21. This changes service keys and schema metadata, not identity-keyed collection semantics."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/reachability.test.ts:176; scratchpad/test/github/reachability.test.ts:227; scratchpad/test/github/resources2.test.ts:1076; scratchpad/test/github/resources2.test.ts:1105",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "Reachability tests read the package manifest beside upstream src. Workflow polling fixtures provide workflow_runs envelopes for discovery and subsequent polls.",
          "labBehaviour": "The lab keeps upstream package.json as github module data, exports ./index.ts and declares Beep runtime dependencies; manifest tests read it inside the module. Workflow fixtures distinguish list discovery from single-run responses after the verified polling fix, retaining completion/timeout assertions and checking status 408.",
          "reason": "test-environment: The 2026-10-09 environment-fix ruling and D9 authorize lab manifest data and equivalent fixtures; env-github.md:24, central-notes.md:13 and repair-github.md:6-10. Fixture repair changes no source behavior."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/reachability.test.ts:29; scratchpad/test/github/reachability.test.ts:164; scratchpad/test/github/reachability.test.ts:168; scratchpad/test/github/reachability.test.ts:222",
          "upstreamBehaviour": "Bundle scanning starts at ../src, expects only effect for Rest/Resilience/GraphQL and searches entrypoint exports ending in .js.",
          "labBehaviour": "Scanning starts at scratchpad/effected/github, normalizes effect/* to effect, includes @beep/identity/packages and GraphQL @beep/utils/Option edges, and checks .ts re-export paths. Manifest assertions still enforce sideEffects=false and declared runtime dependencies.",
          "reason": "reachability: D9 lab-layout retargeting, step 3 per-module import graph and step 4 identity dependencies require equivalent reachability expectations; env-github.md and the reachability S0 diff ground the changes."
        },
        {
          "test": "scratchpad/test/github/GitHubApp.test.ts:352",
