I need to ensure I gather all findings for the user and report them together. The phrase seems complex: "extend structural patch-codec derivation through union members and codec transformations." It feels tough but necessary to preserve those transformations and checks while decoding via the registered codec. Oh, and I should avoid adding stale documents to the backlog if the user wants to omit closed items. The previous inventory didn’t include those documents, so I'm considering the situation carefully.
